What is original, and what is adapted
-------------------------------------
- src/*.py is original work by Sashank Vemuri. career-ops contains no Python
  at all, and these files import none of its modules. (Checked against
  career-ops at the fork point and at current upstream: no 4-line block of
  code is shared with any upstream file, in any language.)

- src/render-pdfs.mjs adapts two functions from career-ops's generate-pdf.mjs:
  normalizeTextForATS() (ATS-safe character normalisation) and convert()
  (font-path rewriting, print settings, page count). They are condensed
  rewrites rather than verbatim copies, but they follow the upstream
  implementation closely, so they are distributed under career-ops's MIT
  licence, whose full text is included in licenses/.

Runtime relationship
--------------------
- The scan stage's optional portal pass (Stage 2 of src/manual-scan.py) runs
  career-ops's scan.mjs, so it only works inside a career-ops checkout. Pass
  --skip-stage2 to scan without it.
- The pipeline reads and writes the on-disk layout career-ops establishes:
  data/pipeline.md, data/jd_cache.json, data/applications.md, reports/,
  batch/tracker-additions/ and output/. Those conventions shaped this tooling,
  and the credit for them belongs upstream.
